                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a fun game at a  Great price. Works perfect on steam deck. I very much appreciate that you can choose between a standard hidden object game or switch it to adventure mode. I like to have a balance and  change of pace. I typically prefer adventure dominant games mostly, with some hidden object list scenes. Sometimes the hidden object scenes go too overboard in some games, for my liking. I prefer a balance. When I saw in the settings that you could completely change between \"hidden object mode\" & \"Adventure mode\" I thought that was a cool feature. I started on adventure mode, but definitely plant to play it on hidden object mode on my next play through. \n\nAt first I thought there was an issue  nearing the end, I am playing on Advanced with no hints, and it really has been hard mostly common sense. Before that I had a problem in the beginning with flashlight placement but other than that it was a great balance, challenging just enough to be enjoyable, but not overly so.  Upon coming up towards the end I really thought my game was bugged and wouldn't allow me to continue. I spent several hours trying like hell to figure out why in the world I wasn't able to continue. I finally broke down and read a study guide with big fish, which made me think that there was definitely a bug. I thought for sure part 2 would be ruined and I wouldn't get to finish the game. Then I was just about to give up and I realized the problem was all me haha. 6 of the skulls were super simple and couldn't really miss them. But I tell you what, the skull that you can only access with the \"monkey wrench\".... That one is one big S.O.B.... I don't see how anyone could find that without any help.\n\nAnyways I really like the game, and the price on sale, you simply couldn't pass it up. Even the normal price is a great price for this game. I definitely recommend. I look forward to starting part 2 later and hopefully can buy part 3 in the coming days. Excellent start to the franchise, can't wait to see what happens next!",
